{"units": [{"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote121", "translation": "the offspring of many-childed Tethys, children of father Ocean, who rolls around the whole earth with sleepless stream"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote122", "translation": "ancient-born Cronus"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote123", "translation": "the smooth fields of Sicily with beautiful fruit"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote124", "translation": "the noble archer-slaying Hymenaeus"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote125", "translation": "great and many-nurturing Nile"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote126", "translation": "ancient Thebes"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote127", "translation": "noble Ariomardus"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote128", "translation": "ancient Athens"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote129", "translation": "great Nile"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote130", "translation": "great Zeus"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote131", "translation": "ivy-crowned Apollo"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote132", "translation": "Thus Pr. 75: the deed is done"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote133", "translation": "For this disease is somehow inherent in tyranny: not to trust friends"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote134", "translation": "such are the rewards, and elsewhere not rarely"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote135", "translation": "What remedy for this disease did you find?"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote136", "translation": "having stolen your flower, he gave it"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote137", "translation": "the many-colored night"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote138", "translation": "the burden of the present evil"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote139", "translation": "the philanthropic character"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote140", "translation": "he betrayed your privilege to mortals, and in a hundred other places"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote141", "translation": "But it is the right time for strangers who have been traveling all day to obtain what is suitable after a long journey"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote142", "translation": "since it is time not to delay any longer"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote143", "translation": "hurry, since it is not time to delay"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote144", "translation": "life, race, earth and land, tongue, divinity, body, house and home, sun, death, god, spirit, head and head, word, mother, fate, form, story, ship, disease, child, father, fatherland and country, multitude, city, toil, foot, roof, army, host, child, hand, earth, and not a few others, examples of all of which, placed either with or without the article, are cited under these words"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote145", "translation": "the much-destroying wandering"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote146", "translation": "the wealthy and gold-rich seats"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote147", "translation": "the first and last runner wins"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote148", "translation": "the remaining prophecies of the god"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote149", "translation": "his own good children, and in the places indicated above and in not a few others"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote150", "translation": "Hades, receiver of the dead"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote151", "translation": "of wretched mortals"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote152", "translation": "having destroyed the whole race"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote153", "translation": "to these new gods"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote154", "translation": "the plan of Zeus"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote155", "translation": "into my chambers"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote156", "translation": "the bed of Zeus"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote157", "translation": "the future time"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote158", "translation": "against my enemies"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote159", "translation": "the spear of Poseidon"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote160", "translation": "your body"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote161", "translation": "the mouth of Zeus"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote162", "translation": "my body"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote163", "translation": "the mighty Erinys of my father"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote164", "translation": "of my rule"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote165", "translation": "but it is said that the gods of the captured city leave it, where I corrected to 'since the gods leave the seats of the captured city'"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote166", "translation": "with the midday heat of the sun"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote167", "translation": "of these prayers"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote168", "translation": "her own child"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote169", "translation": "with his spear"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote170", "translation": "my brother"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote171", "translation": "of all the gods, both those of the city and those of heaven and those of the marketplace"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote172", "translation": "the black king of birds, and the one behind is white"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote173", "translation": "the public herds before, Fate will destroy them by force"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote174", "translation": "the old lord"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote175", "translation": "Zeus, who did these things"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote176", "translation": "the house of the Atreidae"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote177", "translation": "the servant of the young tyrant"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote178", "translation": "the stranger"}, {"id": "articulus_praepositivus-quote179", "translation": "Loxias of Parnassus"}]}